# BORJIE - Docker ignore patterns
#
# IMPORTANT: BuildKit/Docker .dockerignore patterns are matched against the
# path RELATIVE TO THE BUILD CONTEXT ROOT. A bare `node_modules/` therefore
# matches ONLY the top-level dir, NOT nested `apps/*/node_modules`,
# `packages/*/dist`, `apps/*/.next`, etc. In this monorepo those nested
# artifacts total ~7+ GB, which ballooned the Fly build context to ~1 GB+ and
# wedged the remote upload. Every artifact pattern below MUST use the `**/`
# prefix so it matches at any depth. The multi-stage Dockerfile rebuilds
# everything from source (turbo build), so shipping local builds is pure waste.

**/node_modules/
.git/
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
.env.local
.env.*.local
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
**/__tests__/
**/__mocks__/
**/coverage/
**/e2e/
**/e2e-report/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/.blob/
**/dist/
**/.next/
**/.expo/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.turbo/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
Docs/
# api-sdk's `generate` script reads Docs/api/openapi.generated.json
# at build time. The Dockerfile.web COPYs Docs/api/ explicitly so the
# api-sdk build can succeed in the customer-app dep chain.
!Docs/api/
*.md
!README.md
.github/
infra/
